Subject: checksum the tag sequence big-endian

CSUM_V3 gives every descriptor tag a checksum over the journaled block's
contents, seeded with the journal uuid and the transaction's sequence number.
jbd2 checksums cpu_to_be32(sequence); lwext4 checksummed the host-order value.

Self-consistent -- lwext4 verifies its own tags with the same computation --
and wrong for everyone else. The Linux kernel rejects every data block of
every transaction while recovering a journal this code wrote:

    JBD2: Invalid checksum recovering data block 1290 in journal block 711
    JBD2: journal recovery failed
    EXT4-fs (loop0): error loading journal

which means a volume this driver left dirty could not be mounted by Linux at
all. Nothing caught it earlier because the kernel-replay suites ran on mke2fs
fixtures whose journals carry no checksums, and the volumes our own mkfs
formats were only ever handed to the kernel clean.

Same shape as the commit-block checksum fix before it: the journal is
big-endian, everywhere, including inside checksum computations.

With this, the kernel reports "recovery complete" on a torn volume our mkfs
formatted and our writer left dirty.
--- a/src/ext4_journal.c
+++ b/src/ext4_journal.c
@@ -339,8 +339,17 @@
 		/* First calculate crc32c checksum against fs uuid */
 		checksum = ext4_crc32c(EXT4_CRC32_INIT, jbd_fs->sb.uuid,
 				       sizeof(jbd_fs->sb.uuid));
-		/* Then calculate crc32c checksum against sequence no. */
-		checksum = ext4_crc32c(checksum, &sequence,
+		/* Then calculate crc32c checksum against sequence no.
+		 *
+		 * Big-endian, like every field in the journal: jbd2 checksums
+		 * cpu_to_be32(sequence). Checksumming the host-order value made
+		 * every tag verify against lwext4's own recovery and fail
+		 * against Linux's -- "JBD2: Invalid checksum recovering data
+		 * block N", on every block of every transaction, so a journal
+		 * this driver left dirty could not be recovered by the kernel
+		 * at all. */
+		uint32_t seq_be = to_be32(sequence);
+		checksum = ext4_crc32c(checksum, &seq_be,
 				sizeof(uint32_t));
 		/* Calculate crc32c checksum against tho whole block */
 		checksum = ext4_crc32c(checksum, buf,
